# Example — production CORS_ORIGINS for AIOps FastAPI (Vault / backend/.env)
#
# Rules:
# - Exact browser Origin (scheme + host [+ port]), comma-separated
# - No trailing slash
# - https for published hosts (http://… redirects to https on Loft ingress)
# - API reads CORS_ORIGINS at startup → change requires pod restart
# - Front: browser picks API by hostname (corp front → corp API, Cross front → Cross API).
#   See src/lib/api-base-url.ts; Vite bake includes VITE_CORP_* / VITE_CROSS_* + VITE_API_URL fallback.
# - Keep both front origins listed while both fronts are used.
#
# Canonical values live in deploy/published-hosts.env (CORP_* / CROSS_*).
# Keep this example in sync when cutovers change those keys.
#
# Corp (canonical): CORP_FRONT_URL / CORP_API_URL
# Optional Cross Prod (cutover): CROSS_FRONT_URL / CROSS_API_URL

CORS_ORIGINS=https://aiops-app-model.loft-corp.com.br,https://aiops-app-model-front.cross.loft-prod.io

# Local-only (do not rely on these in Vault prod):
# CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:8080,http://127.0.0.1:8080
